From 8a1b7dc24ce02a6cab4b0834bb925bcc92725661 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: xxxvik-xakerxxx <19531907+xxxvik-xakerxxx@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 14:20:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] drm: mediatek: fix MT6878 DSC RC thresholds

drm_dsc_set_rc_buf_thresh() stores the VESA RC buffer thresholds in the
hardware PPS representation after shifting the specification values by six.

The MT6878 encoder programming shifted those bytes a second time.  That
reduced the expected 0x0e, 0x1c, ... table to mostly zeroes and produced an
invalid compressed stream even though the DSI packet framing was correct.

Write the DRM DSC threshold bytes directly.  This matches the single shift
performed by the vendor driver when its input table still contains the
unscaled specification values.

Signed-off-by: xxxvik-xakerxxx <19531907+xxxvik-xakerxxx@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/mediatek/mtk_ddp_comp.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/mediatek/mtk_ddp_comp.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/mediatek/mtk_ddp_comp.c
index e14edc2..f5f5cec 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/mediatek/mtk_ddp_comp.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/mediatek/mtk_ddp_comp.c
@@ -317,7 +317,7 @@ static void mtk_dsc_encoder_config(struct device *dev,
 
 		reg_val = 0;
 		for (j = 0; j < 4 && i + j < DSC_NUM_BUF_RANGES - 1; j++)
-			reg_val |= (dsc->rc_buf_thresh[i + j] >> 6) << (j * 8);
+			reg_val |= dsc->rc_buf_thresh[i + j] << (j * 8);
 		mtk_ddp_write(cmdq_pkt, reg_val, &priv->cmdq_reg, priv->regs,
 			      DISP_REG_DSC_PPS0 + 0x20 + i);
 	}
